# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in what you need.
# `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit real keys.
#
# THE CONTACT FORM WORKS WITH THIS FILE EMPTY. Everything below is an upgrade,
# not a requirement. See "Contact form" in README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Contact form delivery ---------------------------------------------------
# With none of these set, submissions relay through FormSubmit, which needs no
# key: the recipient address is the endpoint. Fine to launch on.
#
# Set ONE of the following to take ownership of delivery. Priority is the order
# they appear in: Resend beats Web3Forms beats the webhook beats the default.

# Option A (recommended) — Resend. https://resend.com
# First-party: your account, your sender, nobody else holding your messages.
#   1. Sign up with sarangprajapati06@gmail.com — that address becomes the only
#      one the free shared sender may deliver to, which is what a contact form
#      needs anyway.
#   2. API Keys -> Create API Key (send-only is enough). Paste it here.
#   3. Done. No domain, no DNS.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Option B — Web3Forms. https://web3forms.com
# Enter your email on their site and the access key arrives by email. No
# password, no account to manage.
# WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# Option C — any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST (Slack or Discord incoming
# webhook, Zapier, your own API route).
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where enquiries land. Defaults to `site.email` in src/data/site.js.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=sarangprajapati06@gmail.com

# Resend only, and only once you own a domain and have verified it in Resend.
# Defaults to "Portfolio <onboarding@resend.dev>".
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL="Portfolio <hello@yourdomain.com>"
